---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReviewedByCard from "../../components/ReviewedByCard.astro";

const title = "Mortgage Payment in DTI Calculations";
const description =
  "How to use the full housing payment (PITI + HOA + PMI) in DTI and affordability checks. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-04-03";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/mortgage-payment-dti-housing-payment" lastUpdated={lastUpdated} robots="noindex, follow">
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">DTI housing payment</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>Mortgage payment in DTI calculations</h1>
    <p>
      DTI should include the full housing payment: principal, interest, taxes, insurance, HOA, and PMI. This guide shows how to
      build that number so your affordability checks are realistic.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">Affordability checklist</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ReviewedByCard
    reviewedBy="Practical Finance Tools Editorial Team"
    reviewerRole="DTI housing-payment inclusion review"
    reviewedOn="2026-04-03"
  />

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Use this guide when your DTI answer depends on the full housing payment</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use this page when the lender's DTI result looks tighter than your own math because taxes, insurance, HOA, or PMI were left out.</li>
      <li>If you need the basic payment structure first, move to <a href="/guides/how-mortgage-payments-are-calculated">how mortgage payments are calculated</a>.</li>
      <li>If the next decision is whether the payment still fits your budget, move next to the <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">mortgage payment affordability checklist</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Mortgage payment inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Loan amount, note rate, and term.</li>
      <li>Taxes, insurance, HOA, and PMI assumptions.</li>
      <li>Escrow rules or reserves used by the lender.</li>
      <li>Time horizon if comparing scenarios.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">What to include</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Principal and interest (P&amp;I).</li>
      <li>Property taxes and homeowners insurance.</li>
      <li>HOA dues if applicable.</li>
      <li>PMI or mortgage insurance if required.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Front-end vs back-end DTI</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Front-end DTI uses the housing payment only. Back-end DTI includes housing plus other required debts. Make sure you know which
      ratio you are comparing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Leaving out taxes or insurance from the housing payment.</li>
      <li>Using a guessed payment instead of a calculator estimate.</li>
      <li>Mixing front-end and back-end ratios in comparisons.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Where to get the numbers</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Loan Estimate or Closing Disclosure for escrow items.</li>
      <li>Property tax bill or county rate estimates.</li>
      <li>Insurance quotes for annual premium estimates.</li>
      <li>HOA documents for dues and assessments.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Why lender math often feels higher than borrower math</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Borrowers often compare DTI using principal and interest only, but underwriting usually works from the full housing payment.
      That means taxes, homeowners insurance, HOA dues, and mortgage insurance can turn a comfortable-looking estimate into a tighter approval ratio.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Inputs to double-check</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Monthly taxes and insurance after escrow adjustments.</li>
      <li>Any PMI or mortgage insurance premium changes.</li>
      <li>HOA dues that increase annually or quarterly.</li>
      <li>Planned rate changes if using an ARM scenario.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Lender DTI target and your comfort threshold.</li>
      <li>Conservative tax and insurance estimates.</li>
      <li>Expected HOA increases or special assessments.</li>
      <li>Income volatility buffer for seasonal work.</li>
      <li>Other debts that may start or end soon.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Scenario checklist</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Base case with current tax and insurance quotes.</li>
      <li>Stress case with higher HOA or PMI assumptions.</li>
      <li>Income drop buffer (one month lower income).</li>
      <li>Rate change scenario for ARM plans.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/how-mortgage-payments-are-calculated">Mortgage payment math</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/front-end-vs-back-end-dti">Front-end vs back-end DTI</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/what-is-piti">What is PITI?</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">Mortgage payment affordability checklist</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">References</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/consumer-tools/mortgages/ready-to-buy-a-home/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Ready to buy a home?
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/owning-a-home/explore/home-loan-toolkit/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Your home loan toolkit
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">Run the DTI calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Estimate the payment</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">Check affordability</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-04-03</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>



